     1	# error-mapping Overview
     2	
     3	Owns Tovu's domain-to-HTTP classification policy. The generic envelope,
     4	serializer and default status mapping already belong to Jini; call them rather
     5	than implementing another version here.
     6	
     7	## Contract to adopt
     8	
     9	Source: `development/todos.md:1514`, triage s4-59 (2026-10-17).
    10	Status: analytics pilot migrated in source; compatible Jini decoder adopted by the admin transport. Tests pass (committed 56a29e396).
    11	
    12	`@jini-ai/protocol` owns `ApiErrorResponse` and `ApiError`:
    13	
    14	```json
    15	{
    16	  "error": {
    17	    "code": "NOT_FOUND",
    18	    "message": "workspace was not found",
    19	    "requestId": "proxy-request-123"
    20	  }
    21	}
    22	```
    23	
    24	`details` (JSON), `retryable` (boolean), and `requestId` (string) are optional
    25	fields inside `error`. `@jini-ai/http-kit` exports `createCompatApiError`,
    26	`sendApiError` and `statusForError`; the installed package already supplies them.
    27	Use `res.locals.requestId` from request tracking for correlation, matching the
    28	response's `x-request-id`. Never mint a second id during error translation.
    29	
    30	The existing Jini status taxonomy includes:
    31	
    32	| Class / code | HTTP status | Caller interpretation |
    33	|---|---|---|
    34	| `BAD_REQUEST` | 400 | Malformed request |
    35	| `UNAUTHORIZED` | 401 | Authentication required |
    36	| `FORBIDDEN` | 403 | Authenticated but action denied |
    37	| `NOT_FOUND` | 404 | Resource absent or outside the workspace |
    38	| `CONFLICT` | 409 | State conflicts with the requested operation |
    39	| `PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE` / `UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE` | 413 / 415 | Request transport rejected |
    40	| `VALIDATION_FAILED` | 422 | Well-formed input fails validation |
    41	| `RATE_LIMITED` | 429 | Respect the server's retry policy |
    42	| `INTERNAL_ERROR` | 500 | Unexpected failure; caller-safe message only |
    43	| `UPSTREAM_UNAVAILABLE` / `SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE` | 502 / 503 | Dependency or capability unavailable |
    44	
    45	Unknown codes default to 500 in Jini. Domain-owned codes remain permitted by
    46	Jini's open code type; preserve an established domain status contract explicitly
    47	rather than assuming a generic default fits it. `retryable` is not permission
    48	to retry a mutation without its existing idempotency contract. Never serialize a
    49	raw exception, stack, SQL, credentials or unreviewed domain payload into `details`.
    50	
    51	## Analytics pilot
    52	
    53	The bounded pilot is `GET /api/admin/v1/workspaces/:workspaceId/analytics/recent-hits`,
    54	registered by `runtime/composition/modules/analytics.ts`. Workspace misses, authorization
    55	refusals and unexpected failures use `NOT_FOUND`, `FORBIDDEN`, `INTERNAL_ERROR` through
    56	`respond.ts`, which calls Jini's serializer/status mapping and reuses `res.locals.requestId`.
    57	Success, workspace-check ordering, permission requirements, denial reason and reviewed
    58	permission details are preserved. Raw exceptions stay out of the envelope.
    59	
    60	`@jini-ai/protocol` now exports `decodeApiError({ body }, { fallbackMessage })` for both
    61	legacy string errors and canonical nested envelopes. `apps/admin/src/lib/api.ts` calls it
    62	for error messages/codes and session invalidation. Only a 401 with `UNAUTHENTICATED`
    63	invalidates the session; an upstream vendor's `UNAUTHORIZED` does not. The original body
    64	remains available through `ApiError.body`, including details/retryability/correlation metadata.
    65	Malformed object messages receive the existing fallback instead of `[object Object]`.
    66	
    67	Source tests cover decoder compatibility, admin transport, the analytics route, the
    68	async-error guard and `respond.ts` correlation. Auth/session and recovery middleware
    69	remain separate migration surfaces. Jini source changes need their normal package
    70	build/publication/adoption before this can run against registry artifacts; none was
    71	performed by this edit-only dispatch.
    72	
    73	## Remaining surfaces
    74	
    75	After analytics, the admin families still to review/migrate are: agent-plugins,
    76	api-keys, assistant, change-sets, comments, commerce, content, content-types,
    77	database, database-recovery, deployments, entries, external-mcp, forms, fs-files,
    78	integrations, media, members, menus, newsletter, pages, plugins, posts,
    79	presentation, publish-content, recovery, redirects, seo, settings, site, sites,
    80	skills, system, taxonomy, themes, trash, users, widgets and workspace.
    81	
    82	Public families are content, external-mcp, members, oauth, ops, publish-trust and
    83	site. Include shared auth/authorization, serving gates, body-parser errors,
    84	fallback 404/500 handlers and plugin-contributed routes in the inventory.
    85	Inspect each contract: streamed/SSE errors and protocol-owned OAuth/MCP failures
    86	must retain their owning protocol's wire format. This is an inventory, not a
    87	claim that every listed surface currently returns a legacy JSON error.
